  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Monday)\nIssued at 1022 AM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nTemperatures currently span the 50s to low 60s across the Mid-\nSouth with high pressure remaining in firm control of our overall\nforecast. A weak, upper-level ridge will continue to build\nthrough the remainder of the week and into the weekend, leaving\nbehind a dry weather pattern as high pressure will continue to\ndominate the forecast. Temperatures are still on track to reach\nthe mid to upper 70s across the area today, with some locations\nrising to the low 80s beginning Wednesday and continuing through\nthe rest of the week. While conditions will certainly still feel\ncomfortable, this will be about 5 to 10 degrees above normal for\nthe end of October as far as high temperatures go. For our\novernight temperatures, lows will vary depending on the location.\nGenerally low lying areas will be closer to the mid to upper 40s,\nwhile locations along and west of the MS River will fall to the\nlow to mid 50s.\n\nThe only concern through the remainder of the week will be the\ncontinued drought conditions and elevated fire danger conditions\nas a result. As such, be sure to obey all local burn bans.\nOutdoor burning and activities that involve open sparks or flames\nare discouraged. For those wondering when we will finally break\nout of this weather pattern, there does not appear to be a clear\nend in sight. Some guidance does want to bring a system towards\nthe middle of next week, but there is still significant\nuncertainty. Thus, it looks like generally above-normal\ntemperatures and no precipitation will remain in the forecast for\nthe next seven days.",
